## 💎 3.7 Simple Exception Handling (try-catch)
* **Exception:** A runtime error that happens while a program is running (e.g., trying to parse letters like "asdf" into a number). Unhandled exceptions crash the program instantly.
* **try-catch Statement:** Prevents crashes by intercepting runtime errors gracefully:
    ```csharp
    try
    {
        // Code that might cause an exception
        miles = double.Parse(milesTextBox.Text);
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        // Code that runs only if an error happens
        MessageBox.Show(ex.Message); // Displays default error text
    }
    ```

